      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but if we're talking about \"effectiveness\" specifically, shouldn't the primary measure be whether the state can actually maintain its sovereignty and control its borders? like, if a country can't control who comes in, isn't the policy technically a failure regardless of the economic side of things?",
